From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:14:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/smmstore: Stop the firmware watchdog before the
 command can fail

The firmware watchdog of a platform is stopped from
smmstore_firmware_confirmed(), which the SMI handler called only once
SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD had gone through: after the parameter
check, after smmstore_init(), and only with VBOOT and VBOOT_VBNV_FLASH.
A store that does not initialize, or a build without the vboot nvdata
in the flash, failed the command before the stop, and the watchdog,
armed in romstage, then reset the OS at every timeout: in a loop when
the slot is confirmed already, as vboot has nothing to fall back to.

The command says that the payload runs, which is all a watchdog over
the firmware needs to know. Call the hook as soon as the command is
seen, before the checks of the command itself.

TEST=Build of the ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init and of the
ThinkCentre M920x.

Change-Id: I94fd818f0636d21ed753742c03b6bab5180697ef
---
 src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 src/include/smmstore.h     |  5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c b/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
index c48a16ae..17f0bd84 100644
--- a/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
+++ b/src/drivers/smmstore/smi.c
@@ -284,8 +284,9 @@ static uint32_t vboot_try_other(void)
 }
 
 /*
- * The payload confirmed the RW slot (SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD): the
- * firmware booted. A platform with a firmware watchdog stops it here.
+ * The payload sent SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD: the firmware booted, whether
+ * or not there is a slot to confirm. A platform with a firmware watchdog
+ * stops it here.
  */
 __weak void smmstore_firmware_confirmed(void) {}
 
@@ -297,6 +298,15 @@ uint32_t smmstore_exec(uint8_t command, void *param)
 	if (smmstore_preprocess_cmd(&command, param))
 		return SMMSTORE_RET_SUCCESS;
 
+	/*
+	 * The payload says that the firmware booted. Told here, before
+	 * anything of the store or of vboot can fail the command: a firmware
+	 * watchdog needs neither to be stopped, and one left running would
+	 * reset the OS at every timeout.
+	 */
+	if (command == SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD)
+		smmstore_firmware_confirmed();
+
 	/* No parameters: coreboot sends it too, on S3 resume */
 	if (command == SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_LOCK) {
 		if (!CONFIG(VBOOT_SLOTS_RW_AB) || !CONFIG(VBOOT_VBNV_FLASH))
@@ -360,7 +370,6 @@ uint32_t smmstore_exec(uint8_t command, void *param)
 			break;
 		}
 		vbnv_mark_tried_slot_good();
-		smmstore_firmware_confirmed();
 		ret = SMMSTORE_RET_SUCCESS;
 		break;
 	case SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_TRY_OTHER:
diff --git a/src/include/smmstore.h b/src/include/smmstore.h
index 563533ae..20391dfd 100644
--- a/src/include/smmstore.h
+++ b/src/include/smmstore.h
@@ -219,7 +219,10 @@ bool smmstore_options_write_allowed(size_t offset, const void *data, size_t size
 struct lb_header;
 void lb_smmstorev2(struct lb_header *header);
 
-/* Called by the SMI handler when the payload confirms the RW slot (weak) */
+/*
+ * Called by the SMI handler at every SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD of the
+ * payload, before the command itself can fail (weak)
+ */
 void smmstore_firmware_confirmed(void);
 
 #endif
-- 
2.43.0

